/-!
# The original full residual is the literal midpoint-span commutator

The endpoint action on the natural midpoint span already consumes the whole
field-sized fixed-preimage index of Q0=[Q_a,L_a]. Hence Q0 is generated by
the fixed preimage and P=[W,L_a]. The original U_a belongs to P because the
midpoint normal span contains Z_a. Thus the endpoint fixes Q0/P. Its
nontrivial image in the original simple symplectic quotient forces the whole
two-residual to fix Q0/P. Residual idempotence gives Q0=P.

Every group and coordinate kernel remains the literal original one. No
natural structure on Q0, splitting, or residual-span identity is assumed.
Source: MS93 (3.10)(i), printed p.880, used in (5.12), printed p.927.
-/

public noncomputable section
